  message: "G1 investigation (read-only, PR #808 session): proposes a shared make_route_symbol minting helper (kind-slot=function + origin/origin_run_id stamping + name-slot=sanitized(node.name)). NOTE: the py.py Starlette line refs in this item (~2752/2782/2812) are STALE — Starlette now lives at py.py:3060-3110 and ALREADY builds its id with kind='function' + Symbol.kind='function' (ADR-0036 Ruling 2), so its KIND-slot fossil is already fixed; remaining on that producer = origin provenance (this item) + the name-slot (WI-vuzaf Pattern B, best folded into the same make_route_symbol chokepoint). Not implemented this pass (multi-producer, own chokepoint decision). Still todo_hard."  # 1dce
- op: discuss  # e61d
  at: '2026-07-29T04:53:18Z'  # e61d
  by: agent  # e61d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e61d
  clock: 5  # e61d
  nonce: e61d  # e61d
  message: "CHOKEPOINT + GATE LANDED (PR #63, dev 7f285e1102). No producer migrated yet --\nthis is the gate-before-sweep half, deliberately separate so each producer\nmigration provably shrinks a measured number.\n\nSHIPPED: `analyze.base.make_route_symbol` -- the shared minting helper this item\nasked for. It encapsulates the shape framework_patterns.materialize_route_symbols\nalready proved for the WI-tufil trio: id via make_symbol_id(kind=\"function\"),\nkind=\"function\", meta[\"framework_role\"], origin + origin_run_id stamped,\nmake_route_stable_id, transport_meta() splitting WS/LIVE/RPC out of the verb\nfield, INV-nimik empty-path normalization. 10 unit tests, 100% cov.\n\nNAMING RESOLVED -- and it was NOT an open decision. WI-vuzaf's note said Pattern B\n\"needs a route-naming decision\"; the decision already exists in the WI-tufil\nprecedent (materialize_route_symbols sets name = \"{METHOD} {path}\"). Adopted, and\nit turns out to be FORCED rather than stylistic: a multi-method registration\n(Starlette methods=['GET','POST'], a Django CBV expanded per verb) emits several\nmarkers at the SAME span, so a handler-derived name-slot would COLLIDE their ids\n-- only the method+path pair is unique by construction. The handler name moves to\nmeta[\"handler_ref\"], which is what linkers/route_handler already resolves against\n(it never read Symbol.name), so this is lossless for the linker. Regression test\npins the collision case.\n\nNEW FINDING -- the gate found a violation INSIDE the cohort WI-tufil declared\nclean. The existing test_route_marker_symbols_are_validator_clean checks three\nproperties (id kind-slot, origin_run_id, origin pass-id) but NOT the id NAME-slot.\nMeasured baseline over fixtures/route-parity:\n   java, javascript -- clean (mint via the materializer)\n   python, rust     -- 0 route markers (routes surface as concept=route on the\n                       handler; py.py's Django/Starlette/Flask-RESTful direct\n                       producers need their OWN fixtures to be gated -- see below)\n   go               -- VIOLATION: go:main.go:8-8:ANY /users:function has\n                       name='listUsers'. go.py mints inline (net/http ~3520,\n                       gorilla chain ~3725, chi/gorilla Mount ~3805) with\n                       name=handler_name against an id name-slot built from\n                       \"{METHOD} {path}\". This is exactly WI-vuzaf's inverted\n                       Pattern B, which WI-vuzaf filed as Starlette-SPECIFIC --\n                       it is fleet-wide, and go is the analyzer-direct producer\n                       the WI-tufil gate leans on as its \"the checks actually\n                       ran\" anchor.\n\nGATE: test_route_marker_id_name_slot_round_trips, parametrized per language, with\nNAME_SLOT_HOLES recording go as a STRICT xfail -- a migration XPASSes and fails\nthe suite, forcing promotion (the ROUTE_HOLES idiom). Deliberately a marker, NOT\nan imperative pytest.xfail(): the imperative form always reports xfail and can\nnever XPASS, so it would have recorded the hole while silently disabling the\nratchet meant to close it (caught before commit).\n\nREMAINING SWEEP (this item stays todo_hard). Producer inventory re-verified live\n-- 11 files, ~22 minting sites: go.py (5), py.py (3: Django/Starlette/\nFlask-RESTful), ruby.py (3), js_ts.py (2), php.py (2), play_routes.py (2:\nroute + route_include), elixir.py (2), swift.py (1), linkers/grpc.py (1),\nannotation_convention.py (1), framework_patterns.py (2, already clean).\nOrder: go FIRST (closes the live gate hole; ~15 test assertions in test_go.py\npin routes[N].name == \"<handlerName>\" and must flip to \"{METHOD} {path}\" -- a\nreal user-visible node.name change for go route markers, lossless via\nmeta.handler_ref). Then py.py, which needs NEW route-parity fixtures (django/,\nstarlette/) since the existing python/ fixture is Flask and produces no marker.\n\nSEPARATE DEFECT found en route, belongs to this group but not this item:\nlinkers/grpc.py:417 has a LOCAL _make_symbol_id emitting\n\"grpc:{file}:{line}:{name}:{kind}\" -- 'grpc' in the lang slot and a BARE LINE\nwhere the canonical grammar wants a {start}-{end} span. That is an INV-dulah\nid_format violation independent of the route-marker shape; recorded on WI-vuzaf\n(which already owns it as residual (b))."  # e61d
- op: discuss  # 4833
  at: '2026-07-29T05:27:03Z'  # 4833
  by: agent  # 4833
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4833
  clock: 6  # 4833
  nonce: '4833'  # 4833
  message: "PRODUCER 1 OF ~10 MIGRATED: go.py (PR #64, dev ef039d29d8).\n\nAll four inline minting sites in go.py -- net/http HandleFunc, gorilla-mux\nbuilder chain, chi/gorilla Handle, framework route path -- now call\nanalyze.base.make_route_symbol.\n\nCONSUMER-VISIBLE CHANGE (disclosed, not incidental): a go route marker's\nSymbol.name goes from the handler name (\"submitHandler\") to \"{METHOD} {path}\"\n(\"POST /submit\"). This aligns go with what java/javascript have emitted since\nWI-tufil -- go was the outlier, and its id name-slot ALREADY carried\n\"{METHOD} {path}\" while Symbol.name carried the handler, which is precisely the\nADR-0036 Ruling 1 violation. Handler identity is preserved in\nmeta[\"handler_name\"], the key linkers/route_handler already resolved against\n(it never read Symbol.name), so route->handler edge recovery is unchanged.\n15 test assertions reading routes[N].name were rewritten SAME-INTENT onto\nmeta[\"handler_name\"] -- they still pin handler identification.\n\nRATCHET DRAINED AS DESIGNED. Sequence, for the record, because it validates the\ngate-before-sweep ordering: (1) gate lands with go as a strict xfail -> 8 passed\n1 xfailed; (2) go migrates -> [XPASS(strict)] -> 1 FAILED, i.e. the suite failed\nON SUCCESS and refused to let a fixed producer stay marked broken; (3) go\npromoted out of NAME_SLOT_HOLES -> 9 passed. Note this only works because the\nhole is a MARKER (pytest.mark.xfail(strict=True)); the imperative pytest.xfail()\nform would have reported xfail at step 2 and left the hole in the file forever.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE, real repo (~/ALL_REPOS/curriculum_repos/caddy, full\n`hypergumbo survey .`): 3 route markers, 0 violations across all four properties\n-- id name-slot round-trips sanitize(Symbol.name), id kind-slot == Symbol.kind,\nnon-empty origin_run_id joining a real AnalysisRun, registered origin pass-id.\nFixture corpus (go/java/javascript) all clean. 11549 passed / 4 skipped, 100%\ncoverage on changed files.\n\nINCIDENTAL, NOT THIS ITEM: caddy's responsewriter.go:68 yields a marker with\nroute_path \"/POST\" (name \"POST /POST\") -- a route-DETECTION false positive,\npre-existing and unrelated to marker identity. Not filed; noted so the next\nperson measuring this corpus does not read it as migration damage.\n\nREMAINING (this item stays todo_hard): py.py (3 sites: Django ~3052, Starlette\n~3083, Flask-RESTful), ruby.py (3), js_ts.py (2), php.py (2), play_routes.py (2),\nelixir.py (2), swift.py (1), linkers/grpc.py (1), annotation_convention.py (1).\nNEXT-STEP BLOCKER for py.py: it needs NEW route-parity fixtures (django/,\nstarlette/) before it can be gated at all -- the existing python/ fixture is\nFlask, which surfaces routes as a concept=route tag on the handler and produces\nno standalone marker (measured: 0 markers). Adding the fixture is what puts the\nproducer under the gate; the migration follows.\n\nPRECEDENT NOTE for whoever continues: each remaining producer migration carries\nthe same consumer-visible node.name change for its language. That is convergence\nonto one convention, but it lands incrementally across the [Unreleased] window --\nworth a single consolidated release note rather than ten scattered ones."  # 4833
- op: discuss  # 7023
  at: '2026-07-29T07:36:00Z'  # 7023
  by: agent  # 7023
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7023
  clock: 7  # 7023
  nonce: '7023'  # 7023
  message: "MEASURED FLEET SURVEY (2026-07-29) — the \"nine producers each carrying a consumer-visible\nnode.name change\" framing from PR #64's writeup is WRONG for most of the fleet. Measured\nlive by running the full pipeline over purpose-built scratch fixtures, not inferred.\n\nTwo distinct violation shapes, not one:\n\nSHAPE A — id KIND-slot fossil only; Symbol.name is ALREADY \"{METHOD} {path}\".\nMigration onto make_route_symbol changes node.id (kind slot) and leaves node.name\nbyte-identical. NOT a consumer-visible rename.\n  ruby (3 sites)   id=ruby:routes.rb:2-2:GET /users:route          name='GET /users'\n  php  (2 sites)   id=php:routes.php:3-3:POST /users:route         name='POST /users'\n  elixir (2)       id=elixir:router.ex:5-5:GET /users:route        name='GET /users'\n  swift (1)        id=swift:routes.swift:4-6:GET /users:route      name='GET /users'\n  grpc (1)         id=grpc:user.proto:5:RPC /demo...:route         name='RPC /demo...'\n  play_routes (1)  route_name = f\"{method} {path}\"                 (source-read, unmeasured)\nIn every case the id kind-slot is the literal 'route' (or 'route_include'/'route_mount'),\nwhich is NOT a registered symbol kind, while Symbol.kind == 'function'. This is the\nWI-tufil kind-slot fossil, still live across the fleet tail — exactly what this file's\nown module docstring at test_route_concept_parity.py already named as the follow-up.\ngrpc additionally emits a NON-CANONICAL 4-segment id (no language slot, single line\nnumber instead of a start-end span): grpc:{file}:{line}:{name}:{kind}.\n\nSHAPE B — id NAME-slot mismatch; migration DOES change node.name.\n  py.py django          name='django:list_users'   id name-slot='/users/'\n  py.py starlette       name='starlette:unknown'   id name-slot='GET /users'\n  py.py flask-restful   name='{view_name}'         id name-slot='{route_path}' (source-read)\n  go   r.Mount()        name='apiRouter'           id name-slot='MOUNT /api/v1'\n\nSo the genuine node.name churn is ~4 sites in 2 producers (py.py, go-mount), not nine\nproducers. The other ~10 sites are pure id kind-slot repair.\n\nNEW FINDING 1 — go is NOT fully migrated. PR #64 migrated go's four make_route_symbol\nsites but MISSED a fifth: the chi/gorilla `r.Mount(\"/api/v1\", handler)` path at\ngo.py:~3780, which still constructs Symbol(...) directly with\n`make_symbol_id(..., f\"MOUNT {prefix}\", \"route_mount\")` and `name=handler_ref`. It\nviolates BOTH the kind-slot property (route_mount unregistered, Symbol.kind='function')\nand the name-slot property. It is invisible to the current gate because the go\nroute-parity fixture is net/http only and contains no Mount call — the same\nunexercised-path blind spot as pt.40(a). Measured live:\n  id=go:main.go:13-13:MOUNT /api/v1:route_mount  name='apiRouter'  -> NAME-SLOT KIND-SLOT KIND-UNREG\nCorrection to the PR #64 note: \"all four inline minting sites migrate / 0 violations\"\nwas true of what the fixture exercises, not of the producer.\n\nNEW FINDING 2 — the Django CBV expander emits a 6-SEGMENT id (hard grammar break).\nSplit out as its own item, see WI-javag.\n\nNEW FINDING 3 — php double-quoted route paths are silently undetected (the php fixture\nemitted zero markers until switched to single quotes). Split out as WI-fadip.\n\nBASELINE — what the gate covers today: 3 markers from 2 producers (go analyzer 1,\nroute-materializer 2 for java+javascript). python and rust route-parity fixtures emit\nZERO standalone markers (they surface concept=route on the handler instead), so they\ncontribute nothing to this gate. Every other producer is entirely ungated.\n\nConsequence for sequencing: the kind-slot sweep (Shape A) is a clean, name-preserving\nbatch that can land independently of the node.name release-communication question,\nwhich only governs Shape B."  # 7023
